      "raw": "<p>This is the ongoing card that reverses the order of the hero turn.&nbsp;&nbsp; If you are under the effect of this card, and you play a card that destroys ongoing cards during your &quot;play a card&quot; phase, does the turn reset at that moment?&nbsp; The &quot;play a card&quot; phase is the second-to-last phase while under the card&#39;s effect.&nbsp;</p><p>Which of these would happen?</p><p>1) You finish your turn as if the card were still there, and the next player takes there&#39;s in the proper order. This is the least likely as the SotM mechanic doesn&#39;t tend to ignore things like that.</p><p>2) The turn resets.&nbsp; Since you were on the second to last phase, you now go to the last phase which would be &quot;end of turn&quot; <em>again</em>, and any &quot;end of turn&quot; effects go off again.</p><p>3) The turn resets.&nbsp; Instead of looking at your position in the turn ordianally, the game looks at it by position name.&nbsp; Since you just finished your &quot;play a card&quot; phase, you are now on your &quot;use a power&quot; phase again.&nbsp; You would get to use a power, draw a card, and trigger end of turn effects again.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thank you for your help.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
