      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-10T15:06:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The turn would continue, from the phase you are currently on.</p><p>The best was Flechettes from an EDU by Omnitron-X.</p><p>The only sad thing was since it doesn't reverse the order cards came into play so we didn't get to use his components twice.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here's a side question to this: &nbsp;With Self-Destruct Sequence sending you to the end of your turn to add a card to the pile, you would go back through to the start of your turn, where you would again have the option to skip your turn.</p><p>Wouldn't this just cause an infinite loop?</p><p>And since that isn't a thing what part would cause it to not be an infinite loop?</p>",
